Đấy thì nó sẽ gen ra nè

337
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:56,820
Mọi người thấy không rất là đẹp nha

338
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,660
Thì anh em có thể ghen lại

339
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,200
Hoặc là ghen khác đi cũng được

340
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,760
Nói chung tùy ý mọi người

341
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,760
Thì em thấy như này khá là ok rồi

342
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,880
Em sẽ chọn cái tấm ảnh bên phải nha mọi người

343
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:08,600
Đó bên phải nè

344
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,140
Em tải về rồi sẽ vào

345
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,860
Canva chỉnh một tí nha mọi người

346
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:14,080
Đó, chỉnh về cái ánh sáng

347
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,400
Một tí

348
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,400
Để cho nó thấy phù hợp

349
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:19,360
Về đúng với kích thước của

350
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:22,160
Cái tỷ lệ là 16.9 nữa nha anh em

351
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,600
Đấy, sau khi ok rồi

352
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,220
Thì mọi người chỉ cần việc lưu lại

353
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,320
Về sức ảnh ra thôi

354
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,480
Rồi bây giờ thì em sẽ cho mọi người xem

355
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:30,880
Về cái demo em vừa làm lúc nãy nha

356
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:34,200
June 4, 1942, Midway Atoll.

357
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:40,280
The humid air trembles with the roar of aircraft engines.

358
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:46,920
In the distance, black smoke rises where burning fuel slicks the Pacific in orange flames.

359
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:53,120
On the deck of the USS Hornet, a handful of new bulky torpedo bombers line up for launch.

360
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:56,600
Their fuselages gleam with fresh paint.

361
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:59,600
TBF Avenger, the Navy calls it.

362
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:06,360
Below deck, 19-year-old radio man James Red Cummings tightens his harness.

363
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:09,280
"Biggest damn bird I've ever seen,"

364
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:13,600
he mutters, patting the steel ribs of the fuselage.

365
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:17,680
The Avenger is massive compared to the older TBD Devastator.

366
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:22,600
Heavier armor, a larger engine, a turret gun.

367
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:27,480
This is its first combat sortie, and few have faith in it yet.

368
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,560
"Remember, she's no fighter,"

369
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:33,600
Lieutenant Langley, the pilot, reminds them.

370
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,280
"We go low and slow.

371
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,760
Make that torpedo count."

372
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:42,160
Above them, Japanese zeros swarm like hawks.

373
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:47,760
On carriers Akagi and Kaga, pilots laugh as they watch the lumbering American torpedo bombers climb off the deck miles away.

374
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:51,800
"Turtles," one pilot snickers in the ready room.

375
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:56,040
"They'll never reach us alive."

376
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:58,840
They were almost right.

377
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:07,800
Out of six Avengers that took off from Midway that morning, five were shot down before reaching their targets.
